INT. DRAINED MUNICIPAL SWIMMING POOL - NIGHT

Cracked blue tile. One work light hums over the deep end. ODALYS VANTERPOOL (30s, night custodian, flashlight like a club) stands on the ladder. BRAM OKONKWO (20s, her apprentice) clutches a mop. PRUDENCE HALE (60s, retired lifeguard, whistle on a cord) and WENDELL DUCROIX (40s, city inspector, clipboard) crowd the rim above.

ODALYS
Nobody swims here. Nobody has swum here since--

PRUDENCE
Since the boy. Say it.

WENDELL
The drain cover is secure, I signed it myself, I signed it twice--

BRAM
Something's knocking. Under the tile.

ODALYS
It's the pipes.

PRUDENCE
It's counting.

Three slow knocks. The work light dies. Odalys and Bram scramble up the ladder, colliding, while Wendell drops the clipboard and Prudence blows the whistle once, hard.

WENDELL
Stop blowing that!

BRAM
Who's laughing? Somebody's laughing!

PRUDENCE
(whispering)
Nobody. Nobody's down there.

The light snaps back on. All four freeze. In the deep end, a single wet footprint, then another, walking toward them.
